WEBVTT

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.780
<i>The match between SC and FC</i>

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.090
<i>ended in a draw, with no resolution.</i>

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.830
<i>There was discussion of a rematch,</i>

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.810
<i>but by Director Kondo's order,</i>

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:14.320
<i>the SC and FC were combined</i>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.320
<i>and Iwaki was appointed Coach</i>

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:20.040
<i>of the new Enoshima High Soccer Club.</i>

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.290
<i>We started training right away 
for the inter-high matches,</i>

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.570
<i>but the team still has a 
few problems to sort out.</i>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.020
<b>Panic at the Training Camp?!</b>

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.700
Damn it! The old maid again!

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:24.120
All right!

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:29.270
<b>King Sized
Snack Bag</b>

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.290
Araki! You dog!

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:33.290
Now, now.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.420
<i>We the Enoshima Soccer Club, 64 strong,</i>

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.800
<i>are heading to a training 
camp in Shizuoka</i>

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.750
<i>for two days and one night,
 to solidify our team.</i>

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.070
<b>King Sized
Snack Bag</b>

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:03.780
Assemble!

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:07.600
H-Hey...

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:16.670
Thank you for having us!

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.130
Thank you for having us!

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.090
Ah, you youngsters have arrived.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:26.100
We've brought quite a few more this time,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.470
so thank you for having us.

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.720
It's nothing. It'll be nice 
and lively, won't it?

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.060
Thank you very much.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:36.580
Such a cute manager, too.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.100
This isn't what I'd expect 
to see in a soccer team.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.990
We've stayed here since 
I worked with the FC.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.470
The price is cheap and the 
soccer field is nearby.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.030
Let's see, you were...?

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:57.690
Oh, come on! You know me. I'm Araki.

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.760
How'd you get that tanuki belly?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:03.380
Leave me alone!

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.700
All right! Bring in the gear.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.640
Okay.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:09.520
Well, excuse me.

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:12.380
I'll be back by tonight,
 so tell everyone...

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.320
Sure.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:14.600
Do your best.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:15.640
Of course!

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:24.070
And that's the first half!

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:27.350
Nadeshiko Japan vs. the 
American Women League's

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:30.700
Miami Hurricanes match reaches 
the end of the first half

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.830
with the Miami Hurricanes in the lead, 2-0.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.790
What's wrong, everyone?

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:38.380
It's only the first half!

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.920
We can get two goals! We can!

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.140
We had many promising plays.

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:43.880
We did.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.940
If we just had someone who could

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.470
break through with a dribble 
and create an opening.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.650
Although it's just a friendly match,

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.780
we're representing Japan.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:55.340
We can't afford to lose.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:55.860
Yes.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.190
I'm sorry for being late!

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.580
Is everything okay with your training camp?

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.310
Yes. I'm sorry I worried you.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:09.800
What do you think you're doing?

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:10.620
I'm sorry!

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.700
I'll definitely get those points 
back in the second half.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:15.760
<i>This girl...</i>

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.000
All right. Go change!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:18.860
Okay!

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:24.470
In the second half,

00:05:24.470 --> 00:05:26.960
Japan makes a change of players.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.820
In for number 17, Ooshita,

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.530
number 7,

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.050
Nana Mishima!

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:38.140
I don't seem to have any 
information about Mishima.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.210
Where could she have come from?

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.650
She seems very young.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.490
Number 10, Ishiki, is 
moving up to forward,

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:46.610
and she appears to be 
filling in below the top.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.430
Director Goto must have 
something up his sleeve.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:53.210
<i>That's a pretty scrawny girl 
they've brought out.</i>

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.230
<i>But where have I seen her before?</i>

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:02.210
I'll have you show me that you're 
more than just talk, Mishima-san.

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:05.420
Otherwise, the director has no place

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:08.420
debuting a no-name 
like you mid-match.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:09.320
Right!

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.900
<i>She doesn't look like she's 
got much physical strength.</i>

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:23.710
<i>How about a shoulder tackle</i>

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:24.980
<i>instead of a hello.</i>

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.990
<i>Hey! I never fail my target!</i>

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:37.370
<i>Wh-Who is this girl?</i>

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:41.220
Amazing!

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:43.530
She avoided a hard attack 
from that big American

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:45.520
like she was nothing more
 than a gust of wind

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.300
and left her in the dust.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.740
Mishima gets past another defender!

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:56.210
How could this be?

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:59.480
<i>A slender body and quick 
and agile movements.</i>

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:00.910
<i>Like a fleeing cat,</i>

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:02.190
<i>she's untouchable.</i>

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.610
Defense! Mark her!

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.780
She won't stop! She's unstoppable!

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:11.910
Number 7, Nana Mishima,

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.630
gets past three defenders on her own

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:15.620
and, before you know it, 
she's brought the ball

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:17.120
just before the penalty area!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:18.540
This could be their chance!

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:19.910
Let's crush her!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.720
Yeah!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.170
But wait!

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:25.210
Two large defenders 
have blocked her path.

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:27.170
Mishima-san! Over here!

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:28.880
Watch out for the others!

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:33.930
What?

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.070
G-Goal!

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:50.020
She surprised the opponents 
with her dribble and

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:52.530
sent the ball right over the 
defender and keeper's heads!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.490
She scores with a truly artful loopshot!

00:07:57.600 --> 00:07:58.830
I did it!

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:01.720
What do you think, Takeda-san?

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:04.970
That shot just now... Takeda-san?

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.210
She's so cute!

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.720
Way to go!

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.090
Nana-chan, right?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:13.450
That loopshot was amazing!

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.070
Thank you so much!

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.940
But we're still down a goal,

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.860
and they're not the type of opponent

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.980
we can out-dribble more than once.

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:24.910
I know.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:26.270
After that play,

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:30.730
my dribble and loopshot should 
be burned into their minds.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.050
So...

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.180
I'm counting on you, Ishiki-san.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.660
What a girl.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.390
All right, everyone.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:46.260
Let's use this momentum 
and tie up the game!

00:08:46.260 --> 00:08:47.500
Yeah!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.720
Never mind. We'll still dominate the game.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.140
I won't let you past here.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:08:59.980
This girl again!

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:02.310
I'm sure I know her from...

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.440
You're open!

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:04.310
Oh, no!

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:06.770
Please!

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:08.240
Oh my!

00:09:08.240 --> 00:09:10.490
Number 7, Mishima takes the ball again.

00:09:08.540 --> 00:09:09.190
No way!

00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.320
But this time they're 
marking her tightly.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.900
It doesn't look like 
she'll get by easily.

00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:15.830
She's really amazing.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.070
She dribbles without even 
glancing at her feet

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:21.290
and keeps the whole field in view.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.340
<i>Shit... Is she trying to get 
past with her dribble?</i>

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:27.670
<i>Or is she going to try 
a long shot from here?</i>

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.630
<i>Here she comes! 
It's a dribble!</i>

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:38.910
Oh! She fakes a dribble 
and passes instead.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:41.670
With the last goal still bright 
in the defenders' minds,

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:44.790
she slips past and sends a through pass

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.230
like a line drawn down a green canvas.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.190
The receiving player 
is number 10, Ishiki!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.450
Come on!

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:58.360
Goooal!

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:02.370
<b>Taeko Ishiki</b>

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.170
It's 2-2. Thirty minutes into the second half!

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:05.370
Nadeshiko Japan's ace, 
Ishiki, puts in the tying goal!

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.580
Nice pass, Nana-chan!

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:08.290
Yeah.

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:11.350
I remember that girl.

00:10:11.350 --> 00:10:12.170
What?

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:14.300
Two years ago,

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:17.560
she debuted in the
 American Premiere League,

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.610
immediately pulled off a hat trick,

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.100
and then disappeared.

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.100
That genius girl,

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.250
the "little witch,"

00:10:24.970 --> 00:10:26.650
Nana Mishima!

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.710
<i>In any case, we can't lose this match!</i>

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.730
One more goal!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:37.420
One more goal!

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:38.900
The nameless Nana Mishima's plays

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:40.990
have really got the crowd excited.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.740
Who could this player, Mishima, be?

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:48.000
Did Japan always have a player like this?

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.380
Over there!

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:51.520
Takeda-san, do you know?

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.420
Takeda-san?

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.330
Mi-shi-ma!

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:55.960
Mi-shi-ma!

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:57.630
She's so cute.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.430
She's so cute.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:02.760
The young striker has brought the 
momentum back to Nadeshiko Japan!

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.720
Their movements have 
improved drastically!

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.670
<i>Your moment in the light is over.</i>

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:12.900
<i>I'll teach you that the "little 
witch" was nothing but a fluke.</i>

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.860
Nana's dribble breaks 
past another defender!

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.150
Stop her! Defend the area!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:23.530
Scissors!

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:27.650
And an elastico!

00:11:27.650 --> 00:11:29.360
Showing off some skilled feints,

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.090
she slips past two defenders

00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.850
and is heading to the area.

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:33.960
<i>I won't let you!</i>

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:37.230
<i>What?!</i>

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:38.630
It's a heel pass!

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.800
And running to meet it is Ishiki!

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.260
Go!

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:48.530
The keeper blocks it!

00:11:48.530 --> 00:11:50.890
The ball goes high. 
There's still a chance.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.350
Here's Mishima with a jumping volley!

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.510
Goooal!

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:04.230
Number 7, Nana Mishima's 
comeback goal is in!

00:12:04.650 --> 00:12:06.670
Almost like magic!

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:10.080
There's the whistle!

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.310
Nadeshiko Japan, 3 to 2!

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:16.000
But who could the striker

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.130
who suddenly appeared, Nana Mishima, be?

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:20.660
Mishima-san,

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.730
you'll play for Nadeshiko 
Japan in the future, right?

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:28.470
I'll come to practice.

00:12:28.470 --> 00:12:30.940
I'll participate in the training camp, too.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:33.480
So please let me continue

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.650
as manager for the
 Enoshima High Soccer Club.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:39.270
Either way, you've taken the first step.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.610
Just think it over as you walk.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.540
Thank you very much!

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:48.220
I've got to get back to the camp!

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:50.200
What about the interview?

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.160
I'm sorry! I'll leave it to you.

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:05.550
They're good!

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.600
Even though South Fujinomiya High

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:10.060
isn't known as a major name in soccer.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:13.790
Shizuoka is called "Japan's Brazil."

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.480
The reason we came here to train

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:19.740
was because highly-skilled 
players are easy to find.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:21.150
I see.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.360
The practice match between Enoshima High

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:28.370
and South Fujinomiya High will now begin!

00:13:29.140 --> 00:13:30.070
Bow!

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:31.870
Thank you for the game!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:35.370
All right. Let's put some goals in.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.820
Looks like they're underestimating 
the nameless Enoshima High.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.900
They'll figure it out soon enough.

00:13:41.900 --> 00:13:42.840
Yeah.

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:47.800
Who's the fatty?

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:49.390
Don't underestimate us!

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.560
Kaoru!

00:14:07.060 --> 00:14:08.510
H-Hey...

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.420
I'm counting on you three!

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.340
<i>It's just a practice match,</i>

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.130
<i>but I'm excited to be wearing</i>

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.600
<i>a uniform and standing on the field.</i>

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.270
<i>I want...</i>

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:36.730
<i>I want to score!</i>

00:14:41.290 --> 00:14:43.140
All right!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.170
Sorry for being late.

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:20.410
Welcome back.

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:24.280
...and so, please give it your all

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.950
at tomorrow's practice, as well.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:26.730
Yeah!

00:15:27.080 --> 00:15:28.570
I'm hungry.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.040
Mmm... smells good.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.190
Let's eat! Let's eat!

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:33.270
Let's stuff ourselves

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:34.890
and have lots of energy for tomorrow.

00:15:35.890 --> 00:15:37.090
Here you go.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.440
What is this?

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:41.680
Your dinner.

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:42.850
Eat up.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:45.620
This is an offering at a Buddhist temple.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:49.090
I want to eat an enormous 
serving of rice.

00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:49.930
You can't.

00:15:50.980 --> 00:15:53.490
You had such a great workout,

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:55.550
so try to live with a smaller meal.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:57.800
This isn't just smaller.

00:15:57.800 --> 00:15:58.470
Is it?

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:05.230
Fine. I just have to diet, right? Diet!

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:07.480
Fine, fine. I get it.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:11.400
<i>Even my side dishes are smaller!</i>

00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:15.050
<i>Shit. You think I'll stand for this?</i>

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.620
<i>Just watch.</i>

00:16:17.010 --> 00:16:19.170
He's flying! He's got it!

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:22.830
Oh! It's payback time.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:32.680
No one's even noticed.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:36.300
All right. I'll just help myself to 
tons of juice and cup ramen.

00:16:36.300 --> 00:16:37.440
Wha—

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:38.680
What is this?

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.470
Who would do something like...

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:42.490
Araki-senpai.

00:16:44.410 --> 00:16:46.050
I thought it was you!

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:47.640
How dare you?!

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:49.270
<b>Apple Juice</b>

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:49.270
Please drink this.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:51.270
Th-That's...

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:53.240
I had good intentions, but...

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:55.770
This is too much, isn't it?

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.240
Please drink this.

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:02.710
Take it away.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.120
Senpai?

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:07.190
The real match is coming up,

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:10.500
but I'm still a ways 
away from my top form.

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.280
So you do understand!

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:14.610
Yeah. So go.

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:16.680
Leave that juice,

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:18.120
I'll throw it away.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:19.100
Okay.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:20.480
Then...

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:29.330
As if! I'll be drinking this!

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.730
Oh, I forgot to mention.

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.200
That's an herbal laxative.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:39.050
Bitter! What is this?

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:42.120
It's apparently great for dieting 
since it relieves constipation.

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.440
It's coming out!

00:17:48.050 --> 00:17:50.730
She really is no ordinary girl, is she?

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:51.500
Y-Yeah.

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.870
I'm so hungry!

00:17:54.870 --> 00:17:56.470
I'm sorry, Araki-san.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.030
Seven is desperate, too.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:02.700
She's trying everything to get 
you into the best condition.

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:06.130
I'm not letting that girl 
get away with this.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:08.900
Women's Bath

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:08.660
Nana-chan, I'm heading back first.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:09.860
Take your time, okay?

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:16.820
Women's Bath

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:12.260
Okay, Senpai.

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:14.420
Mishima is by herself?

00:18:14.420 --> 00:18:15.560
In the bath?

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:16.820
Do you want to?

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:18.700
I'm doing it!

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:21.790
I'll be peeking as payback 
for the dieting.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:24.390
H-Hey! You mustn't peek.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:25.460
Shut up!

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.010
I'm already pissed off.

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:28.830
Let's go, all of you.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.280
Yeah!

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.210
You can't!

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:35.170
This way.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.280
Ko-Kota!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:39.640
What an overlap!

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:50.490
H-Hey! You can't do this.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:50.980
Shh!

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:56.080
H-Hey. Will it open?

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:58.220
This type will open.

00:18:59.610 --> 00:19:01.570
If we all look at once, we'll get caught.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.870
Let's go one-by-one in 
ten second intervals.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.760
I'm calling you the 
conductor of the night.

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:08.120
You can't.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:09.250
Shut up, you!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.580
Whoa! Amazing!

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:12.360
Did you see it?

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:14.090
No, just the back.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:18.050
Turn around. Turn around.

00:19:18.710 --> 00:19:20.680
<i>Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.730
<i>I'm just going to have to yell...</i>

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:24.470
You guys!

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:28.440
I thought something was fishy,

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:30.810
so I followed you, and what do I find?

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.950
Oh, shit! Run!

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:40.470
Honestly. What if we were to get 
in trouble for something like this?

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:41.990
Is someone there?

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:57.260
You're peeking!

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:59.100
Oda-san, you pervert!

00:19:57.490 --> 00:20:00.170
W-Wait! You don't understand!

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:01.120
Jerk! I hate you!

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:02.390
Just let me explain!

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.440
Someone help!

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:08.270
You're wrong!

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:14.530
After this, it is finally 
time for the much awaited

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:16.570
annual test of courage!

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.570
Yeah!

00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.690
The test of courage will be held

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:23.770
at the shrine in the 
hills behind the lodge.

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:26.800
The first years may not know this,

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.680
but there's an interesting history 
associated with that shrine.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:31.750
Right?

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:34.510
Yes!

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:40.800
That shrine is commonly 
called the Kemari Shrine.

00:20:40.820 --> 00:20:44.000
The ghosts of the nobles 
who lost at Kemari

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:45.870
appear there every night, calling,

00:20:45.870 --> 00:20:48.940
"Kemari... Pon!"

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:51.660
"Pon!"

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:51.660
This story again.

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:52.680
It seems so contrived.

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:53.890
It isn't scary at all.

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.210
Kakeru, are you okay?

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:01.160
Y-Yeah.

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.500
The team who goes up the mountain

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:07.230
and finds the hidden 
lantern is the winner.

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:09.420
Every year, the player who takes

00:21:09.420 --> 00:21:13.120
the lantern may or may not 
become great at soccer.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:17.580
Then, starting with the first group, 
come draw from the hat.

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:22.140
I'm counting on you to make things 
interesting this year, as well.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:25.720
You're with us.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:26.460
What?

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.980
All right. We're first.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:39.440
Get out of the way!

00:21:41.010 --> 00:21:43.230
The lantern is mine!

00:21:43.230 --> 00:21:44.100
It's mine!

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:46.130
Mine!

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:47.460
No, mine!

00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:49.410
They're on the same team...

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:49.410
Mine!

00:21:58.010 --> 00:21:59.640
Where's the lantern?

00:22:13.150 --> 00:22:14.980
Th-That voice...

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:24.610
Let's play Kemari.

00:22:24.990 --> 00:22:28.070
I-I-It's real!

00:22:46.000 --> 00:22:48.550
Reproachful!

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:53.660
I found it!

00:22:57.610 --> 00:23:00.120
Araki... I've wo—

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:08.740
I got it!

00:23:10.350 --> 00:23:11.820
Show us!

00:23:12.750 --> 00:23:14.000
H-Hold it!

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:15.410
Get back here!

00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:18.880
No! Stay away!

00:23:21.230 --> 00:23:22.250
No!

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:25.650
They seem to be having fun.

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:28.490
Yes, this is as it should be.

00:23:37.440 --> 00:23:40.690
Now I'm even hungrier.

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:46.140
It's not a joke!

00:23:53.160 --> 00:23:54.580
The wind feels good.

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:00.670
The Enoshima Soccer Club

00:24:00.670 --> 00:24:02.560
is finally on its way.

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:03.440
Yeah.

00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:06.000
I'll have to do my best as well.

00:24:10.610 --> 00:24:11.970
Don't worry.

00:24:12.430 --> 00:24:13.870
You'll be fine.

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:16.550
We'll do our best together.

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:20.610
Seven?

00:24:45.940 --> 00:25:15.390
<b>Next Episode: 
Little Witch</b>

00:24:46.970 --> 00:24:49.960
Nana stands on the field once 
again for Nadeshiko Japan

00:24:49.960 --> 00:24:52.920
against the German Pro
 League, SF Frankfurt's Ace,

00:24:52.920 --> 00:24:54.900
Mina Meier.

00:24:54.900 --> 00:24:56.490
Nadeshiko Japan 
struggles against

00:24:56.490 --> 00:24:58.420
the world-class opponent.

00:24:58.420 --> 00:25:01.310
Despite the conflicted 
feelings in Kakeru's chest,

00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:02.650
he's moved by the sight of

00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:06.980
Nana fighting earnestly, 
 without hesitation.

00:25:07.370 --> 00:25:09.020
Next time on
Knight in the Area,

00:25:09.020 --> 00:25:11.540
episode 10: "Little Witch."

00:25:11.540 --> 00:25:14.360
Kakeru, I won't 
run away, either.
